     NetHack's Qt interface is willing and able to handle a command
line if you choose to give it one.  To do that, you'll need to use a
terminal window instead of the mouse.

     The config file that was called defaults.nh (or nethack.cnf if
you go back far enough) on MSDOS and Windows is called .nethackrc
on Unix (including Mac OSX) and it resides in your home directory
rather than in nethack's directory.  Under OSX you can also use
Library/Preferences/Nethack Defaults
(note the embedded space) or
Library/Preferences/Nethack Defaults.txt
and it is an ordinary text file regardless of which name you pick.

     Including ``OPTIONS=name:player'' or ``OPTIONS=name:games''
in your config file should cause the game to issue the "who are you?"
prompt.



